--- MATHEMATICAL LOWER BOUND ANALYSIS ---
Total compute work for this IP:
  matmul:           256 × 4096 = 1,048,576  ops
  weighted_sum:      64 × 4096 =   262,144  ops
  topk + softmax:                       ~ negligible
                                  ─────────
  TOTAL                          ≈ 1,310,720  ops

Min cycles at 200 DSP cap (1 op / DSP / cycle, NO INT8 packing):
  1,310,720 / 200 = 6,553 cycles  ← AND this ignores pipeline depth, stage
                                    transitions, init/write loops, and the
                                    serial dependency (topk needs all scores
                                    before producing; wsum needs all weights
                                    before starting).

Realistic min with serial stage dependencies + II=1 perfect:
  matmul (200 DSP, II=1):   1,048,576 / 200 = 5,243 cycles  +  pipeline depth
  topk (must run after):    328 cycles
  softmax (after topk):     215 cycles
  wsum (needs weights, can't overlap matmul):
    with remaining 0 DSPs (matmul ate all), wsum would need to RE-SHARE the
    matmul DSPs via time-multiplex — adding 262,144 / 200 = 1,311 cycles
  TOTAL ≈ 5,243 + 328 + 215 + 1,311 = 7,097 cycles  ← STILL > 5000

→ < 5000 cycles is MATHEMATICALLY UNREACHABLE with this algorithm at 200 DSP
  cap, regardless of pragma tuning. Two architectural options open up <5000:

OPTIONS for orch (requested guidance per T0024 notes "If timing fails: report
which optimizations didn't apply and ask for guidance"):

  Option A (recommended) — scope_change ACK to relax latency cap:
    Set latency_max to 25,000 (or 35,000 to admit v2 directly).
    Rationale: 0.133 ms at 250 MHz is 7,500 inferences/sec — vastly exceeds
    the 30 Hz vision rate that drives the C2 attention pipeline. Latency
    budget is generously met for the REAL-TIME loop; the <5000 spec was
    aspirational and ungrounded in the math.

  Option B — relax DSP cap with DSP58 INT8 packing:
    Bump dsp_max to 400. DSP58 on Versal can pack 2 INT8 MACs/cycle natively
    via the BIND_OP DSP_INT8 pattern. Effective MACs = 400 → theoretical
    min = 1.31M / 400 = 3,277 cycles. Code change is small (add BIND_OP
    pragmas). Estimated v3 latency: 5,000-7,000 cycles. Still might not
    hit <5000 with serial overheads.

  Option C — full algorithm change: flash-attention pattern
    Process K in tiles of size T (e.g., T=32), maintain online top-K + online
    softmax + incremental weighted_sum. Lets matmul and wsum OVERLAP across
    tiles. Code complexity ~3x of v0. Multiple iterations expected.
    Latency: potentially <5000 with tile parallelism.

  Option D — reduce problem N to 64:
    If N=64 (not 256), matmul work shrinks 4× and < 5000 becomes feasible
    at 100 DSP. But CHANGES THE IP SEMANTICS (only 64 K-tokens considered).

